<p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-2 dark:text-ink-2-on-dark">
  Four parties, and only four.
</p>

<div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
  <%# The registry API is not on this list, and that is deliberate rather than an
      omission. Searching ClinicalTrials.gov sends the condition and the location,
      which come from the profile, so it is worth saying that the query carries
      those two fields and nothing that identifies anyone. %>
  <div class="rounded-card border border-line dark:border-line-on-dark bg-surface dark:bg-surface-on-dark p-5 flex flex-col gap-1.5">
    <p class="text-base font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-on-dark">A study team, only when you send your details</p>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-3 dark:text-ink-3-on-dark">
      You choose the study and you make contact, using the coordinator's own details on the study page.
      The app does not transmit anything to a study team on your behalf. Once you have sent something,
      what you sent is theirs, and their own privacy terms apply to it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-card border border-line dark:border-line-on-dark bg-surface dark:bg-surface-on-dark p-5 flex flex-col gap-1.5">
    <p class="text-base font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-on-dark">Anthropic, to rewrite a study description</p>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-3 dark:text-ink-3-on-dark">
      When you ask for a plain-language version of a study, that study's public registry text is sent
      to Anthropic's API. Nothing about you goes with it, and the result is cached against the study
      rather than against your account, so everyone who opens that study sees the same summary.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-card border border-line dark:border-line-on-dark bg-surface dark:bg-surface-on-dark p-5 flex flex-col gap-3">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
      <p class="text-base font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-on-dark">ClinicalTrials.gov, when you search</p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-3 dark:text-ink-3-on-dark">
        A search sends the condition and the location it is searching on, which come from your profile
        when you are signed in. Nothing that identifies you is part of the query, and the registry has
        no account for you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-card border border-line dark:border-line-on-dark bg-surface dark:bg-surface-on-dark p-5 flex flex-col gap-3">
    <p class="text-base font-bold text-ink dark:text-ink-on-dark">Our hosting provider</p>
    <%= render Pages::DraftComponent.new(
          label: "the hosting provider",
          waiting_on: "Name the host and say what they hold, which is the database and the logs. " \
                      "This is the only one of the four that is a company nobody has heard of, " \
                      "so naming it is the point."
        ) %>
  </div>
</div>

<p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-2 dark:text-ink-2-on-dark">
  We do not sell your information, and we do not share it with advertisers or data brokers.
</p>
